rent hand and possible melds. Since I have no melds, I need to decide which tile to discard to maximize future possibilities. \n\nMaybe the safest tile is T3 or T4, as they are part of the previous player's meld and less likely to be needed. \n\nBetween those, I'll choose to discard T3. So the answer is Play T3.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Discarding T3 is a strategic move as it is part of the previous player's existing meld [T3, T4, T5], reducing the likelihood of others needing it. This maintains flexibility in forming All Terminals and Honors or other patterns while minimizing the risk of aiding opponents' melds.\nReason: T3 is already in the previous player's meld, making it safe to discard. Removing non-terminal tiles like T3 helps progress toward a high-value pattern like All Terminals and Honors (32 points) or Seven Pairs. Other options like W7 or T4 are also viable, but T3 has the lowest risk of being useful to others.\nAnswer: Play T3"}
