not help form a winning hand. Passing maintains concealment and allows flexibility for future draws.\n\nReason: Penging W7 only adds 1 point (Pung of Terminals) and likely prevents higher-value patterns like Fully Concealed Hand (4 points) or All Chows. The current hand lacks sufficient melds to meet the 8-point minimum even with Peng. Passing preserves the potential for higher-scoring combinations by retaining concealed tiles.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
